//? Title: Dinic’s Maximum Flow: Blocking Phases, Cancellation and Cut Checks
//? Subtitle: Actual BFS levels and residual pushes, the original 7.5 example, and the classic flow of 23
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Given a directed network with capacities and distinct source and sink,
we want the largest flow that respects every edge limit and conserves flow
at intermediate vertices. A route chosen early may need to be undone before
other routes can carry more flow. Dinic’s algorithm groups pushes into
blocking-flow phases on residual BFS levels. We begin with the original
single edge of capacity 7.5, then inspect an actual cancellation path that
requires a second phase. The classic six-vertex network reaches value 23,
checked against its per-edge feasibility and cut capacity. Controlled path
families expose phase and current-arc work. Positive capacities below the
old absolute cutoff, bounded trace capture, an iterative long-path traversal
and explicit arithmetic failures make the numerical limits visible.
)

\toc

> One edge: retain the original answer and expose the residual pair

The original executable sends flow from vertex 0 to vertex 1 on one edge
of capacity 7.5. Its unique maximum flow is 7.5. Before the push, the
forward residual is 7.5 and the paired cancellation residual is zero.
The bottleneck is 7.5; afterwards those values are zero and 7.5. The
terminal BFS cannot reach the sink, so the source side of the minimum cut
is {0}, and the crossing capacity is also 7.5.

The new trace records those actual operands and both BFS searches, rather
than rerunning the algorithm at selected prefixes. The same program scales
the single edge over four capacity units. The former fixed residual test
capacity>1e−12 returned zero for 7.5e−13; the canonical kernel now uses
strict positivity and returns that positive flow. It does not introduce
an absolute unit-dependent cutoff.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dinic_single_edge.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::dinic_max_flow_trace(2,{{0,1,7.5}},0,1,8);
  const auto c=dm::algorithms::max_flow_certificate(2,t.network.edges,0,1,t.result);
  const auto& push=t.augmentations[0];const auto& arc=push.path[0];
  std::print("Original flow {:.1f}; edge flows {}; cut side {}; cut capacity {:.1f}; optimal {}.\n\n",t.result.max_flow,t.result.edge_flow,t.result.min_cut_source_side,c.cut_capacity,c.optimal_within_tolerance);
  std::print("| phase | sink level (2 = unreachable) | pushed paths | flow before | flow after |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<t.phases.size();++i){const auto& phase=t.phases[i];std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {:.1f} | {:.1f} |\n",i,phase.sink_level,phase.augmentation_count,phase.flow_before,phase.flow_after);}
  std::print("\nActual pair update: forward {:.1f} to {:.1f}; cancellation {:.1f} to {:.1f}; amount {:.1f}.\n\n",arc.residual_before,arc.residual_after,arc.paired_before,arc.paired_after,push.amount);
  std::print("| capacity | returned flow | cut capacity | duality gap | optimal at zero tolerance |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- |\n");
  for(double scale:{1e-200,1e-13,1.,1e200}){const double capacity=7.5*scale;
    const std::vector<dm::algorithms::CapacityEdge> edges{{0,1,capacity}};const auto r=dm::algorithms::dinic_max_flow(2,edges,0,1);
    const auto check=dm::algorithms::max_flow_certificate(2,edges,0,1,r);
    if(r.max_flow!=capacity || !check.optimal_within_tolerance)return 1;
    std::print("| {:.1e} | {:.1e} | {:.1e} | {:.0f} | {} |\n",capacity,r.max_flow,check.cut_capacity,check.duality_gap,check.optimal_within_tolerance);}
  dm::graphics::Diagram diagram(80,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=3.7;box.height=2;box.font_size=24;
  diagram.node("s",{0,0},"Source 0\ncut side S",box).node("t",{8,0},"Sink 1\noutside S",box)
   .edge("s","t",std::format("flow / capacity = {:.1f} / 7.5",t.result.max_flow))
   .text({4,2.2},"One push saturates the edge and reaches the cut bound",25)
   .text({4,-2.1},std::format("Forward residual {:.1f} → {:.1f}; paired cancellation {:.1f} → {:.1f}",arc.residual_before,arc.residual_after,arc.paired_before,arc.paired_after),22)
   .save_svg("build/dinic_single_edge.svg");
}
```
