\caption(The original single-edge flow reaches 7.5, exactly matching its cut capacity. The recorded residual pair and scale table expose the push and removal of the old absolute cutoff.)
\alttext(Source and sink boxes are connected by a saturated capacity-7.5 edge; a label shows forward residual falling to zero and cancellation residual rising to 7.5.)

> Flow conservation and residual cancellation

For each original arc e=(u,v) with capacity c_e, retain its own flow f_e
with 0<=f_e<=c_e. Net outflow is zero at every vertex except source s
and sink t; the value is net outflow from s, also net inflow to t.
Parallel and antiparallel input arcs keep separate identities. Each input
arc gets a forward residual c_e−f_e and a paired reverse residual f_e.
A reverse push cancels previous flow on that particular original arc.
It is distinct from a separately supplied opposite-direction input arc.

BFS assigns each reachable residual vertex its shortest arc-count distance
from s, considering only positive residual capacities. During a phase,
DFS follows arcs whose head is exactly one level beyond the tail.
The level graph is acyclic. A blocking flow leaves no residual s-to-t
path advancing through those fixed levels: every such path has lost an
available arc. This need not be a maximum-flow solution when rerouting
is allowed. The next example makes that distinction concrete.

There are two left vertices L1,L2 and two right vertices R1,R2. Unit arcs
connect s to each left vertex, L1 to R1 and R2, L2 to R1, and each right
vertex to t. Input order first selects s→L1→R1→t. That blocks all
remaining forward paths in the first level graph, at flow one. A second
BFS finds the length-five residual path
s→L2→R1→L1→R2→t. Its R1→L1 arc cancels the earlier L1→R1 flow.
The two final matches are L1→R2 and L2→R1, giving value two.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dinic_cancellation.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const std::vector<dm::algorithms::CapacityEdge> edges{{0,1,1},{0,2,1},{1,3,1},{1,4,1},{2,3,1},{3,5,1},{4,5,1}};
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::dinic_max_flow_trace(6,edges,0,5);const auto& a=t.augmentations[1];
  const std::vector<std::string> name{"s","L1","L2","R1","R2","t"};
  std::print("Final flow {:.0f}; original L1-to-R1 flow {:.0f}; L1-to-R2 {:.0f}; L2-to-R1 {:.0f}.\n\n",t.result.max_flow,t.result.edge_flow[2],t.result.edge_flow[3],t.result.edge_flow[4]);
  std::print("| phase | actual BFS levels | sink distance (6 = unreachable) | augmentations | flow after |\n| ---: | :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<t.phases.size();++i){const auto& p=t.phases[i];std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {:.0f} |\n",i,p.levels,p.sink_level,p.augmentation_count,p.flow_after);}
  std::print("\n| second-push arc | original edge | cancellation | used residual before | after | paired before | after |\n| :--- | ---: | :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(const auto& e:a.path)std::print("| {} to {} | {} | {} | {:.0f} | {:.0f} | {:.0f} | {:.0f} |\n",name[e.from],name[e.to],e.input_edge,e.reverse,e.residual_before,e.residual_after,e.paired_before,e.paired_after);
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(65,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle node;node.width=1.8;node.height=1.3;node.font_size=23;
  std::vector<std::size_t> vertices{a.path.front().from};for(const auto& e:a.path)vertices.push_back(e.to);
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<vertices.size();++i)d.node(std::to_string(vertices[i]),{3.2*i,0},name[vertices[i]],node);
  for(const auto& e:a.path){dm::graphics::DiagramStroke stroke;stroke.color=e.reverse?dm::graphics::RGB{234,88,12}:dm::graphics::RGB{37,99,235};stroke.width=3;
    d.edge(std::to_string(e.from),std::to_string(e.to),e.reverse?"cancel 1":"push 1",stroke);}
  d.text({8,2},"Second actual residual path: undo one earlier match",25)
   .text({8,-2},std::format("Original L1 → R1 flow becomes {:.0f}; total flow increases from {:.0f} to {:.0f}",t.result.edge_flow[2],a.flow_before,a.flow_after),21)
   .save_svg("build/dinic_cancellation.svg");
}
```
