> Controlled phase growth and measured work

Two canonical generated families separate path multiplicity from path
length. In the first, p internally disjoint unit-capacity paths all have
length four: E=4p and V=2+3p. BFS finds them at the same sink level,
and one blocking phase pushes all p units. In the staircase family,
there is one unit path of each length 1,...,p. Then
E=p(p+1)/2, V=2+p(p−1)/2 and each successful phase removes exactly
the next shortest path. Its successive sink levels are 1,...,p.
This tests increasing phase counts while remaining below the general
V−1 bound; it is not a tight worst-case construction.

Counters include BFS visits to reverse and zero-capacity residual arcs of
reached vertices. DFS inspections include retries of still-current arcs
after successful pushes. The identity J+L separates permanent pointer
movement from the successful path work. Both charts use the executed
counts, rather than values inferred from graph size.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dinic_phase_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");std::vector<double> sizes,equal_phases,stair_phases,equal_checks,stair_checks;
  std::print("| paths | family | vertices | edges | value | blocking phases | BFS searches | DFS inspections | pointer advances | path updates |\n| ---: | :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t paths:{1u,2u,4u,8u,16u,32u}){
    sizes.push_back(paths);
    for(bool stair:{false,true}){const auto g=stair?dm::algorithms::dinic_staircase_paths(paths):dm::algorithms::dinic_disjoint_paths(paths,4);
      const auto t=dm::algorithms::dinic_max_flow_trace(g.vertex_count,g.edges,g.source,g.sink);
      if(t.result.max_flow!=paths || t.work.blocking_phases!=(stair?paths:1) || t.work.dfs_arc_inspections!=t.work.current_arc_advances+t.work.path_arc_updates)return 1;
      std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {:.0f} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",paths,stair?"staircase":"equal length four",g.vertex_count,g.edges.size(),t.result.max_flow,t.work.blocking_phases,t.work.bfs_calls,t.work.dfs_arc_inspections,t.work.current_arc_advances,t.work.path_arc_updates);
      (stair?stair_phases:equal_phases).push_back(t.work.blocking_phases);(stair?stair_checks:equal_checks).push_back(t.work.dfs_arc_inspections);
    }
  }
  auto p=dm::graphics::RPlot::create(),q=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.line(sizes,equal_phases,"equal length",{37,99,235}).points(sizes,equal_phases,"",{37,99,235},5).line(sizes,stair_phases,"staircase",{220,38,38}).points(sizes,stair_phases,"",{220,38,38},5).title("Successful blocking phases").x_label("number of disjoint paths").y_label("actual phase count").y_limits(0,43);
  const double top=1.3*(*std::max_element(stair_checks.begin(),stair_checks.end()));
  q.line(sizes,equal_checks,"equal length",{37,99,235}).points(sizes,equal_checks,"",{37,99,235},5).line(sizes,stair_checks,"staircase",{220,38,38}).points(sizes,stair_checks,"",{220,38,38},5).title("Actual current-arc inspections").x_label("number of disjoint paths").y_label("DFS residual-arc tests").y_limits(0,top);
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(p).add(q).size(1100,520).title("Same number of paths; different path lengths and network sizes").fit_panels().save_svg("build/dinic_phase_work.svg");
}
```
