> Feasibility, optimality and finite arithmetic are separate checks

A feasible flow of seven on a capacity-ten edge is not optimal: its cut
bound is ten and its gap is three. Conversely, a reported value equal to
a cut bound can accompany an infeasible per-edge assignment. Deliberately
supply flow three on 0→1 and flow two on 1→2, both with capacity three,
while reporting value three and cut {0}. The scalar gap is zero, but
vertex 1 accumulates one unit and the sink receives only two. The
independent check rejects feasibility and optimality. The following figure
illustrates that supplied invalid record, not a Dinic output.

A tolerance of 0.5 would accept a feasible value 9.5 against a cut of ten
within that tolerance; the displayed gap remains 0.5. These flags are
numerical checks of the supplied result. They do not replace independent
exact tests when a proof over exact integer data is needed.

The kernel checks every residual pair and cumulative flow before a positive
push. Nonfinite sums raise overflow_error. A positive update lost to
rounding raises runtime_error; for example, trying to subtract one from
an edge residual of 1e100 cannot change that double. No partial flow or
trace is returned. There is no hidden unit-dependent epsilon or automatic
rescaling. The original four-argument name, advanced_graph.hpp include
path and MaxFlowResult layout remain available.

Trace storage is explicitly bounded. If P includes the final failed BFS,
A is the number of augmentations and L sums successful path lengths,
the entry cost is C=P(V+1)+A+L: each phase, each stored vertex level,
each augmentation and each path-arc snapshot counts one. Original graph,
result and working arrays are outside that optional history budget.
The default cap is one million entries; zero disables only that cap.
The single-edge trace costs eight entries exactly; seven fails before
the final BFS. Capture adds O(C) time/storage to the ordinary algorithm.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dinic_checks.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::print("| supplied record | tolerance | flow | cut | conservation error | value error | signed gap | feasible | optimal within tolerance |\n| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- | :--- |\n");
  for(double value:{7.,11.,9.5}){const double tolerance=value==9.5?.5:0;const dm::algorithms::MaxFlowResult r{value,{value},{0}};
    const auto c=dm::algorithms::max_flow_certificate(2,{{0,1,10}},0,1,r,tolerance);
    std::print("| single edge | {:.1f} | {:.1f} | {:.1f} | {:.1f} | {:.1f} | {:.1f} | {} | {} |\n",tolerance,value,c.cut_capacity,c.max_conservation_error,c.value_balance_error,c.duality_gap,c.feasible,c.optimal_within_tolerance);}
  const dm::algorithms::MaxFlowResult bad{3,{3,2},{0}};const auto c=dm::algorithms::max_flow_certificate(3,{{0,1,3},{1,2,3}},0,2,bad);
  std::print("| broken conservation | 0.0 | 3.0 | {:.1f} | {:.1f} | {:.1f} | {:.1f} | {} | {} |\n\n",c.cut_capacity,c.max_conservation_error,c.value_balance_error,c.duality_gap,c.feasible,c.optimal_within_tolerance);
  std::size_t cap=0,overflow=0,progress=0,invalid=0;
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::dinic_max_flow_trace(2,{{0,1,7.5}},0,1,7);}catch(const std::length_error&){++cap;}
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::dinic_max_flow(2,{{0,1,1e308},{0,1,1e308}},0,1);}catch(const std::overflow_error&){++overflow;}
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::dinic_max_flow(3,{{0,1,1e100},{1,2,1}},0,2);}catch(const std::runtime_error&){++progress;}
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::dinic_max_flow(4,{{2,3,std::numeric_limits<double>::infinity()}},0,1);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++invalid;}
  if(cap!=1 || overflow!=1 || progress!=1 || invalid!=1 || c.feasible || c.optimal_within_tolerance)return 1;
  std::print("Expected rejections: history cap {}; total overflow {}; lost residual progress {}; unreachable nonfinite edge {}.\n",cap,overflow,progress,invalid);
  const auto g=dm::algorithms::dinic_disjoint_paths(1,20000);const auto t=dm::algorithms::dinic_max_flow_trace(g.vertex_count,g.edges,g.source,g.sink);
  std::print("Iterative chain: {} edges, flow {:.0f}, longest pushed path {}, BFS arc visits {}, DFS arc tests {}.\n",g.edges.size(),t.result.max_flow,t.work.max_path_edges,t.work.bfs_arc_inspections,t.work.dfs_arc_inspections);
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(75,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle node;node.width=2.8;node.height=1.6;node.font_size=23;
  d.node("s",{0,0},"Source 0\nsends 3",node).node("middle",{5,0},std::format("Vertex 1\nimbalance {:.0f}",c.max_conservation_error),node).node("t",{10,0},"Sink 2\nreceives 2",node)
   .edge("s","middle","flow 3 / capacity 3").edge("middle","t","flow 2 / capacity 3")
   .text({5,2.3},"Supplied invalid record: cut minus reported value is zero",25)
   .text({5,-2.3},"Conservation and terminal balance fail, so the equality does not certify a maximum flow",20)
   .save_svg("build/dinic_checks.svg");
}
```
